(1. Generalized Coordinates & Constraints) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.18 rg
(Real mechanical systems often subject particles to geometric constraints \(holonomic\).) Tj T*
(Using generalized coordinates q_1, q_2, ..., q_n reduces the equations of motion to) Tj T*
(the actual degrees of freedom, bypassing unknown constraint forces.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 12.5 Tf
0.08 0.22 0.4 rg
(2. Hamilton's Principle of Stationary Action) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.18 rg
(The actual trajectory followed by a dynamic system between two configurations at times) Tj T*
(t_1 and t_2 is one that renders the action functional stationary: delta S = 0,) Tj T*
(where the action S is the time integral of the Lagrangian L = T - V.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 12.5 Tf
0.08 0.22 0.4 rg
(3. Derivation of Euler-Lagrange Equations) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.18 rg
(Applying the calculus of variations to delta S = 0 with fixed boundary variations) Tj T*
(yields: d/dt\(del L / del q_dot_j\) - \(del L / del q_j\) = 0 for each coordinate.) Tj T*
T*
